       starts with -- or if the --ll option is used, the shell is assumed to be a
       login  shell and the shell reads and executes the contents of //eettcc//pprroo‐‐
       ffiillee, $$HHOOMMEE//..pprrooffiillee and $$EENNVV if they exist and are readable.

       If the EENNVV parameter is set when the shell starts (or, in the  case  of
       login shells, after any profiles are processed), its value is subjected
