       following tokens: &&&&, ||||, &&, ||&& and ;;.  The first two  are  for  condi‐
       tional execution: _c_m_d_1 &&&& _c_m_d_2 executes _c_m_d_2 only if the exit status of
       _c_m_d_1  is  zero;  |||| is the opposite — _c_m_d_2 is executed only if the exit
       status of _c_m_d_1 is non‐zero.  &&&& and |||| have equal precedence  which  is
       higher than that of &&, ||&& and ;;, which also have equal precedence.  The
       &&  token  causes  the  preceding command to be executed asynchronously,
