              _npp     paste the contents of the yank buffer just after the cur‐
                     rent position, _n times.

              _nPP     same as pp, except the buffer is pasted at the current po‐
                     sition.

       Miscellaneous vi commands

              ˆˆJJ and ˆˆMM
                     the  current  line  is  read,  parsed and executed by the
                     shell.

              ˆˆLL and ˆˆRR
                     redraw the current line.

              _n..     redo the last edit command _n times.

              uu      undo the last edit command.

              UU      undo all changes that have been made to the current line.

              _i_n_t_r and _q_u_i_t
                     the interrupt and quit terminal characters cause the cur‐
                     rent line to be deleted and a new prompt to be printed.

